THE POST-MODERN MIRROR  
Young people ơ responded to Pulp Fiction because it reflects the postmodern 
artistic sensibility they grew up with. Post-mode rnism · result of a world blown apart, 
fragmented into millions of pieces by a century of war, social disruption, and rapid 
technological change. The doors of perception č shattered by machines ° 
frantic pace of electronification. Young people now come to awareness in a high-intensity 
bombardment of random images and brief story segments torn from ő previous styles of 
