Young people perceive ń as reflections in a shattered mirror, whether they 
channel-surf to cut up the stories É or have the stories chopped up ¹m by 
MTV-style editing. ầ accustomed to juggling story lines, time periods, and genres at 
staggering speed. Because ¡ archival nature of television, constantly churning images 
and eras, post-modern kids live hi a stew of styles. The young can costume É hi 
fashions  
