Pulp Fiction is postmodern also in its sense of cultural relativity. Although the f ilm is set 
in America, it is shot through Ä sense of worldwide culture and a global viewpoint. The 
characters are constantly comparing one culture to  another, one set of standards to another. 
Jules and à discuss the peculiar way American fast food is named and consumed in 
other countries, and marvel at drug laws in other lands. õ, the American boxer, compares 
notes Ä South American woman cabdriver on personal names in different cultures-her 
