As writers we travel to other worlds not as mere daydreamers, but as shamans with 
the magic power to bottle up those worlds an d bring them back ¤ form of stories 
for others to share. Our stories have the power to heal, ş ń new again, 
to give people metaphors by ūy  Ãtter underst°ir own lives.  
When we writers apply the ancient tools of  the ø and ª 
to modern stories, we stand ¶ shoulde rs ¡ mythmakers and shamans of old. 
When we try to heal our people ² wisdom of myth, we are the modern 
